comment.narrative:
Development of up to six SOPs per border service;  

Organisation of up to six thematic trainings per border services; 

Organisation of up to four regional workshops for border services; 

Development of up to six SOPs per jurisdiction for criminal police; 

Organisation of up to six thematic trainings for criminal police per jurisdiction;

Organisation of up to four regional workshops for criminal police.

description.narrative:
 Security upgrade of one storage location ongoing;
 Security of up to nine (9) evidence rooms increased;
 Up to 3,100 pieces of conventional weapons destroyed.
 Organization of one thematic workshop on ammunition stockpile management.

 Organization of up to two (2) regional meetings of the SALW Commissions;
 Organization of up to two (2) regional meetings of SEEFEN, focusing on networking and information exchange between law enforcement firearms experts;
 Enhancement of capacities of SALW Commissions and SEEFEN members through targeted training sessions and the provision of technical and advisory support;
 Enabling of information exchange, knowledge transfer and standardisation of approaches;
 Publication of quarterly monitors and In-Focus publications on armed violence trends throughout the SEE region;
 Ensuring data collection, analysis and dissemination from authorities based on SALW Survey recommendations;
 On‐demand support for harmonisation of arms control legislation for relevant amendments regarding EU legislation on arms control and standardisation throughout the SEE region;
 Support for integration of gender perspective in SALW policy‐making;
 Facilitating knowledge exchange and information‐sharing with the authorities of Ukraine.

 Provision of equipment for suppression of illicit arms trafficking for border services in two (2) jurisdictions;
 Organisation of one (1) regional workshop for border services;
 SOPs endorsed by five (5) criminal police services;
 Procurement of equipment finalized for six criminal police services;
 Organisation of (1) regional workshops for criminal police services

comment.narrative:
Security of one storage location enhanced in accordance with international standards and best practices; 

Security of up to 18 evidence rooms increased; 

A total of up to 12,000 pieces of conventional weapons destroyed;
